cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VEDA in your work, please cite it, together with the data sets and instrument papers listed by the Cite panel in the app."
title: "VEDA: Visualization, Exploration, and Data Analysis - A Multi-Mission Planetary Science Data Laboratory"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aggarwal
    given-names: Keshav
    email: keshavaggarwal2310@gmail.com
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-02
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  VEDA is a desktop laboratory for planetary atmosphere and ionosphere profiles. It
  searches the official archives (NASA PDS, ESA PSA, JAXA DARTS, ISRO ISSDC) and the
  instrument teams' research data repositories by body, mission and date, reads PDS3 and
  PDS4 products, derives thermodynamic quantities with propagated random and systematic
  uncertainties, compares and averages profiles of several missions with standard errors
  and bootstrap intervals, and computes observation geometry with SPICE. Builds for
  Windows, macOS and Linux.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jovian-explorer/VEDA"
keywords:
  - planetary science
  - planetary atmospheres
  - radio occultation
  - PDS
  - SPICE
